+# STORY-012 — Feature Specification: Target Finance / Settlement Ingest
+
+**Phase:** 6 (Design)
+**Scope:** Medium
+**Date:** 2026-04-29
+**Selected approach:** A — Single-Table Daily Poll (analysis.md, weighted 4.55/5.00)
+
+---
+
+## 1. Overview
+
+Poll Target's `GET /sellers/v1/sellers/{seller_id}/payouts_search` endpoint on a daily cron schedule, normalize Stripe-format payout records into a single Postgres `payouts` table, and index Stripe IDs (`po_*`, `txn_*`, `card_*`) for cross-channel finance reconciliation queries.
+
+**Read-only story.** No writes to Target APIs. Production data access requires explicit operator approval.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Domain Boundaries
+
+| Domain | Responsibility | Boundary |
+|--------|---------------|----------|
+| `app.finance` | Payout ingestion, storage, cross-reference queries | Owns `payouts` table; no cross-domain writes |
+| `app.core` | Shared config, DB session, base client | Provides `settings`, `get_db_session`, `BaseTargetClient` |
+
+`app.finance` imports from `app.core` only. No other domain imports from `app.finance`.
+
+---
+
+## 3. Architecture
+
+### 3.1 Components
+
+```
+┌─────────────────────────────┐
+│  Cron Scheduler (daily)     │
+│  app.finance.poll           │
+│  - ingest_once()            │
+└────────────┬────────────────┘
+             │
+             ▼
+┌─────────────────────────────┐
+│  TargetFinanceClient        │
+│  app.finance.client         │
+│  - fetch_payouts(           │
+│      created_after,         │
+│      created_before)        │
+└────────────┬────────────────┘
+             │ HTTP GET
+             ▼
+┌─────────────────────────────┐
+│  Target API (external)      │
+│  GET /sellers/v1/sellers/   │
+│    {seller_id}/payouts_search│
+└─────────────────────────────┘
+             │
+             ▼
+┌─────────────────────────────┐
+│  Payout ORM Model           │
+│  app.finance.models         │
+│  - upsert into Postgres     │
+└────────────┬────────────────┘
+             │
+             ▼
+┌─────────────────────────────┐
+│  Postgres: payouts table    │
+│  B-tree: id, balance_txn,   │
+│  destination_account        │
+└─────────────────────────────┘
+```
+
+### 3.2 Data Flow
+
+1. Cron triggers `ingest_once()` daily.
+2. `ingest_once()` reads `last_poll_timestamp` from `poll_state` table (or defaults to 30 days ago on first run).
+3. `TargetFinanceClient.fetch_payouts(created_after=last_poll_timestamp)` calls Target API.
+4. Each `Payout` record is upserted into Postgres by natural key `id` (Stripe `po_*`).
+5. Unknown `status` values (anything besides `paid`) are preserved in `status` column as-is and flagged via a `status_known` boolean column (`False` for unrecognized values). Ingest continues without error.
+6. `last_poll_timestamp` updated to `max(created_date)` from the batch (or `now()` if batch is empty).
+
+### 3.3 Failure Modes
+
+| Dependency | Unavailable Behavior | Rationale |
+|------------|---------------------|-----------|
+| Target API | Fail-closed: log error with correlation ID, retry on next daily cron cycle. Do not persist partial results from a failed batch. | Financial data requires atomicity — partial ingest creates reconciliation discrepancies. |
+| Postgres | Fail-closed: crash with structured error log. | Cannot operate without storage. |
+| `TARGET_PROD_API_KEY` env var | Fail-closed: refuse to start poll. Log missing-credential error. | Production credential must be explicitly provided; never fall back to hardcoded values. |
+
+---
+
+## 4. Database Schema
+
+### 4.1 `payouts` Table
+
+| Column | Type | Constraints | Notes |
+|--------|------|------------|-------|
+| `id` | `VARCHAR(255)` | `PRIMARY KEY` | Stripe payout ID (`po_*`). Natural dedup key. |
+| `arrival_date` | `TIMESTAMPTZ` | `NOT NULL` | When funds arrive at destination |
+| `created_date` | `TIMESTAMPTZ` | `NOT NULL` | When payout was created by Target/Stripe |
+| `payout_amount` | `NUMERIC(12,2)` | `NOT NULL` | **Not float.** Exact decimal for financial data. |
+| `currency` | `VARCHAR(3)` | `NOT NULL`, default `'USD'` | ISO 4217 currency code |
+| `description` | `TEXT` | `NULL` | Free-text (e.g., "STRIPE PAYOUT") |
+| `balance_transaction` | `VARCHAR(255)` | `NULL` | Stripe txn ID (`txn_*`) |
+| `destination_account` | `VARCHAR(255)` | `NULL` | Stripe destination (`card_*`) |
+| `status` | `VARCHAR(50)` | `NOT NULL` | Free-text, not enum. Only `paid` documented. |
+| `status_known` | `BOOLEAN` | `NOT NULL`, default `True` | `False` when status is not in known set `{paid}` |
+| `type` | `VARCHAR(50)` | `NULL` | Only `card` documented |
+| `seller_id` | `VARCHAR(255)` | `NOT NULL` | Seller identifier used in the API call |
+| `ingested_at` | `TIMESTAMPTZ` | `NOT NULL`, default `now()` | When this row was first written |
+| `updated_at` | `TIMESTAMPTZ` | `NOT NULL`, default `now()` | Last upsert timestamp |
+
+### 4.2 Indexes
+
+| Name | Columns | Type | Rationale |
+|------|---------|------|-----------|
+| `pk_payouts` | `id` | B-tree (PK) | Dedup key, cross-reference by payout ID |
+| `ix_payouts_balance_transaction` | `balance_transaction` | B-tree | Cross-reference: find payout by Stripe transaction ID |
+| `ix_payouts_destination_account` | `destination_account` | B-tree | Cross-reference: find payouts by destination account |
+| `ix_payouts_created_date` | `created_date` | B-tree | Windowed polling queries, time-range finance reports |
+| `ix_payouts_seller_id` | `seller_id` | B-tree | Multi-seller support if needed |
+
+### 4.3 `poll_state` Table
+
+| Column | Type | Constraints | Notes |
+|--------|------|------------|-------|
+| `poll_key` | `VARCHAR(100)` | `PRIMARY KEY` | e.g., `finance_payouts` |
+| `last_poll_timestamp` | `TIMESTAMPTZ` | `NOT NULL` | High-water mark for `created_after` |
+| `updated_at` | `TIMESTAMPTZ` | `NOT NULL`, default `now()` | |
+
+This is a simple high-water-mark table shared across poll-based ingest stories. If another story (e.g., STORY-011 Returns) ships first and creates this table, reuse it.
+
+### 4.4 Migration Strategy
+
+- Single Alembic migration: `alembic/versions/NNN_target_finance.py`
+- Creates `payouts` table and `poll_state` table (if not exists)
+- Idempotent: `op.create_table` with `if_not_exists` semantics for `poll_state`
+- Run `alembic heads` after creation to verify single head (parallel worktree safety)
+
+---
+
+## 5. API Client Design
+
+### 5.1 `TargetFinanceClient` (`app/finance/client.py`)
+
+```python
+class TargetFinanceClient:
+    """Read-only client for Target payout data."""
+
+    def __init__(self, base_url: str, api_key: str, seller_id: str):
+        # httpx.AsyncClient injected for testability
+        ...
+
+    async def fetch_payouts(
+        self,
+        created_after: datetime | None = None,
+        created_before: datetime | None = None,
+    ) -> list[dict]:
+        """
+        GET /sellers/v1/sellers/{seller_id}/payouts_search
+
+        Returns raw payout dicts from Target API.
+        Raises TargetAPIError on non-2xx response.
+        """
+        ...
+```
+
+**Key design decisions:**
+- Async client using `httpx.AsyncClient` (matches project stack direction)
+- DI-friendly: constructor accepts `base_url`, `api_key`, `seller_id`
+- Returns raw dicts (not ORM models) — separation between API and persistence
+- No retry logic in client; caller (`ingest_once`) handles retry semantics
+
+### 5.2 Authorization — Single Enforcement Point
+
+Authorization is handled by a single function: `app.core.auth.get_target_credentials() -> TargetCredentials`. This function:
+1. Reads `TARGET_API_KEY` (staging) or `TARGET_PROD_API_KEY` (production) from env
+2. Validates the key is non-empty
+3. Returns a `TargetCredentials` dataclass with `api_key`, `seller_id`, `environment`
+
+All code paths in `app.finance` route through `get_target_credentials()`. No module reads env vars directly.
+
+### 5.3 Implementation Patterns (Adapter Interactions)
+
+| Concern | Design |
+|---------|--------|
+| **Parameter binding** | `httpx` query params via `params={"created_after": iso_str}` — no string interpolation |
+| **Error handling** | `httpx.Response.raise_for_status()` → caught as `httpx.HTTPStatusError` → wrapped in `TargetAPIError(status_code, detail, correlation_id)` |
+| **Query generation** | All Postgres queries via SQLAlchemy ORM. Parameterized. No raw SQL string interpolation. |
+| **Pagination** | Target API does not document pagination for `payouts_search`. If response is truncated (heuristic: response contains exactly a round number like 100/500 items), log a warning. Do NOT implement client-side pagination unless Target documents it (OQ-19). |
+
+---
+
+## 6. Poll Logic (`app/finance/poll.py`)
+
+### 6.1 `ingest_once()`
+
+```
+async def ingest_once(db: AsyncSession, client: TargetFinanceClient) -> IngestResult:
+    1. Read last_poll_timestamp from poll_state (key='finance_payouts')
+       - If missing: default to now() - 30 days
+    2. Call client.fetch_payouts(created_after=last_poll_timestamp)
+    3. For each payout in response:
+       a. Validate id matches po_* regex (warn + continue if not)
+       b. Set status_known = (status in KNOWN_STATUSES)
+       c. Upsert into payouts table ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE
+    4. Update poll_state.last_poll_timestamp = max(created_date) from batch
+    5. Return IngestResult(inserted=N, updated=M, skipped=0, unknown_statuses=K)
+```
+
+All steps within a single DB transaction. If any step fails, entire batch rolls back.
+
+### 6.2 Constants
+
+```python
+KNOWN_STATUSES = {"paid"}
+STRIPE_PAYOUT_ID_REGEX = re.compile(r"^po_[a-zA-Z0-9]+$")
+STRIPE_TXN_ID_REGEX = re.compile(r"^txn_[a-zA-Z0-9]+$")
+STRIPE_CARD_ID_REGEX = re.compile(r"^card_[a-zA-Z0-9]+$")
+```
+
+Regex validation is advisory (warn + continue), not rejecting. Target may change ID formats.
+
+### 6.3 CLI Entry Point (`app/finance/cli.py`)
+
+```
+python -m app.finance.cli ingest-once --env staging
+python -m app.finance.cli ingest-once --env production --dry-run
+```
+
+- `--env`: selects credential source (`TARGET_API_KEY` vs `TARGET_PROD_API_KEY`)
+- `--dry-run`: fetches and validates but does not persist. Logs what would be written.
+
+---
+
+## 7. Error Handling Design
+
+### 7.1 Error Response Format (RFC 7807)
+
+All errors surfaced by `app.finance` follow RFC 7807 Problem Details:
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "/problems/finance/target-api-error",
+  "title": "Target API Error",
+  "status": 502,
+  "detail": "GET /sellers/v1/sellers/{seller_id}/payouts_search returned 503",
+  "instance": "/finance/ingest"
+}
+```
+
+Content-Type: `application/problem+json`
+
+### 7.2 Error Classification
+
+| Error | HTTP Status | Logged Context | Not Exposed |
+|-------|-------------|---------------|-------------|
+| Target API 4xx | 502 (upstream error) | operation, seller_id (redacted last 4), status_code, correlation_id, timestamp | Stack traces, API key, full seller_id |
+| Target API 5xx | 502 | Same as 4xx + retry_eligible=True | Same |
+| Target API timeout | 504 | operation, timeout_ms, correlation_id | Same |
+| DB connection failure | 503 | operation, db_host (redacted), correlation_id | Connection string, credentials |
+| Missing credential | 500 | env_var_name, environment | Credential value |
+| Payout validation warning | N/A (not an error) | payout_id (redacted), field, expected_pattern, actual_value (redacted) | Full Stripe IDs |
+
+### 7.3 Fallback Behavior
+
+| Scenario | Behavior | Rationale |
+|----------|----------|-----------|
+| Target API unavailable | **Fail-closed.** Log error, exit. Retry on next daily cron cycle. | Financial data; partial ingest is worse than no ingest. |
+| DB unavailable | **Fail-closed.** Crash with structured error. | Cannot operate. |
+| Unknown payout status | **Continue.** Set `status_known=False`, persist record. | Data is still valuable; unknown status is metadata, not corruption. |
+| Stripe ID format mismatch | **Continue with warning.** Persist record. Log redacted warning. | Format may evolve; rejecting records loses data. |
+| Empty API response | **Continue.** Update poll timestamp. Log info-level "zero payouts in window". | Expected in staging and between payout cycles. |
+
+### 7.4 Logging
+
+All log entries are structured JSON with these fields:
+
+| Field | Always Present | Description |
+|-------|---------------|-------------|
+| `timestamp` | Yes | ISO 8601 |
+| `level` | Yes | INFO, WARN, ERROR |
+| `event` | Yes | e.g., `finance.ingest.started`, `finance.ingest.completed`, `finance.api.error` |
+| `correlation_id` | Yes | UUID per ingest run |
+| `seller_id_last4` | When applicable | Last 4 chars of seller_id only |
+| `records_fetched` | On completion | Count |
+| `records_upserted` | On completion | Count |
+| `unknown_statuses` | On completion | Count of `status_known=False` records |
+
+**Stripe IDs are PII-adjacent.** Never log full `po_*`, `txn_*`, `card_*` values. Log redacted form: `po_...{last4}`.
+
+---
+
+## 8. Operational Readiness
+
+| Concern | Design Decision | Acceptance Criteria |
+|---------|----------------|---------------------|
+| **Health check** | `app.finance` registers a `/health/finance` sub-check that verifies: (1) DB connectivity, (2) `poll_state` table exists | AC: `/health/finance` returns `{"status": "ok"}` when DB is reachable |
+| **Metrics** | Expose counters: `finance_ingest_total` (label: status=success/error), `finance_ingest_records` (label: action=inserted/updated), `finance_ingest_duration_seconds` histogram | AC: After ingest run, counters increment correctly |
+| **Structured logging** | JSON logs with correlation_id per ingest run (see 7.4) | AC: Every ingest run produces structured JSON logs with all required fields |
+| **Alerting** | Alert on: (1) `finance_ingest_total{status="error"}` > 0 for 3 consecutive runs, (2) `finance_ingest_records` = 0 for 7 consecutive production runs | AC: Alert rules defined; documented in runbook |
+| **Runbook** | Document: "Target payout ingest failure" — check Target API status, verify credentials, check poll_state for stuck timestamp | AC: Runbook exists at `docs/runbooks/finance-ingest.md` |
+
+---
+
+## 9. Security Constraints
+
+| Constraint | Enforcement |
+|-----------|-------------|
+| Read-only API access | `TargetFinanceClient` has no write methods. Only `GET` requests. |
+| Production credential isolation | `TARGET_PROD_API_KEY` env var only. Never committed to code. `get_target_credentials()` single enforcement point. |
+| Stripe ID redaction in logs | All log formatters redact Stripe IDs to `{prefix}...{last4}` pattern |
+| No production calls in tests | `respx` mock + explicit assertion: zero outbound HTTP to `api.target.com` or `stage-api.target.com` (except through mock) |
+| Credential audit | Phase 6b `security-review.md` must verify production credential is scoped to GET-only operations |
+
