+
+## 14. Key Design Decisions
+
+| Decision | Choice | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|-----------|
+| Single table, no xref join | `payouts` table mirrors API schema 1:1 | Payout→balance_transaction→destination_account is 1:1, not 1:N. Indexed columns serve cross-reference without joins. |
+| `NUMERIC(12,2)` for amount | Exact decimal, not float | Financial data; floating-point rounding is unacceptable |
+| Status as free-text + `status_known` flag | Not an enum column | Only `paid` is documented; Target may add statuses. Enum would reject unknown values. |
+| Daily poll cadence | Once per day via cron | Payouts settle on banking schedules (T+2). Intraday polling adds API load with no freshness benefit. |
+| Upsert on `Payout.id` | `ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE` | Handles re-delivery and status updates idempotently |
+| No Stripe API enrichment | Out of scope | Seed explicitly defers. Cross-reference via indexed IDs is sufficient. |
+| Async client (`httpx.AsyncClient`) | Matches project direction | Greenfield project; start async from day one to avoid wrapping later |
