+# Phase 8 Implementation — STORY-012: Target Finance/Settlement Ingest
+
+**Date:** 2026-04-30
+**Status:** Complete — 91/91 tests GREEN (was 50 passed, 41 xfailed)
+**Commit:** `1cc024c`
+
+---
+
+## Summary
+
+Implemented the three stubs left by Phase 7 and the CLI entry point:
+
+| File | Status | What Changed |
+|------|--------|-------------|
+| `app/core/auth.py` | ✅ Implemented | `get_target_credentials()` reads env vars, raises `CredentialError` on missing/empty |
+| `app/finance/client.py` | ✅ Implemented | `fetch_payouts()` makes real HTTP GET, maps errors to `TargetAPIError` |
+| `app/finance/poll.py` | ✅ Implemented | `ingest_once()` full poll→normalize→upsert cycle |
+| `app/finance/cli.py` | ✅ Created | CLI entry point for daily cron |
+
+---
+
+## Implementation Details
+
+### `app/core/auth.py` — `get_target_credentials()`
+
+- Reads `TARGET_API_KEY` (staging) or `TARGET_PROD_API_KEY` (production)
+- Raises `CredentialError` if env var is missing OR empty string
+- Reads `SELLER_ID` from env
+- Returns `TargetCredentials(api_key, seller_id, environment)` dataclass
+- Logs structured error on failure (event=`finance.credential.missing`, env_var_name, environment)
+
+### `app/finance/client.py` — `TargetFinanceClient.fetch_payouts()`
+
+- Builds URL: `{base_url}/sellers/v1/sellers/{seller_id}/payouts_search`
+- Omits `created_after`/`created_before` params when `None` (Gate 1 — no "None" strings)
+- Sends `x-api-key` header
+- `httpx.TimeoutException` → `TargetAPIError(status_code=504)`
+- `httpx.HTTPStatusError` → `TargetAPIError(status_code=<actual>)`
+- Every `TargetAPIError` carries a `correlation_id` (UUID)
+- When `http_client=None`, creates a fresh `httpx.AsyncClient()` per call
+
+### `app/finance/poll.py` — `ingest_once()`
+
+Full poll cycle:
+1. Create session from `_engine` (module-level, patched in tests)
+2. Read `PollState` high-water mark; default to `now() - 30 days` on first run
+3. Call `_client.fetch_payouts(created_after=...)` — on `TargetAPIError`: log ERROR, return `{poll_status:"error"}` without touching DB
+4. Empty batch → update `poll_state` to `now()`, return `{poll_status:"empty"}`
+5. For each payout:
+   - Advisory Stripe ID validation (`po_*` regex) — WARN + continue, never reject
+   - Compute `status_known = status in KNOWN_STATUSES`
+   - `session.get(Payout, id)` → UPDATE if exists, INSERT if not
+   - Track `max(created_date)` for poll-state advance
+6. Update `poll_state.last_poll_timestamp = max(created_date)` (or `now()` if all dates null)
+7. `session.commit()` — single transaction covering steps 5+6
+8. Log `finance.ingest.completed` with structured fields (correlation_id, records_fetched, records_upserted, unknown_statuses)
+9. Return observability dict: `{poll_status, records_fetched, records_inserted, records_updated, records_skipped, unknown_statuses, duration_ms}`
+
+**Upsert strategy:** `session.get(Payout, pk)` + conditional update/insert.
+Dialect-agnostic — works for both SQLite (tests) and PostgreSQL (production).
+`ingested_at` is preserved on second ingest; only `updated_at` advances.
+
+### `app/finance/cli.py` — CLI entry point
+
+```
+python -m app.finance.cli ingest-once --env staging
+python -m app.finance.cli ingest-once --env production --dry-run
+```
+
+Wires credentials → client → engine → `ingest_once()`. `--dry-run` fetches but does not persist.
+
