+# STORY-012 — Security Review: Target Finance / Settlement Ingest
+
+**Phase:** 6b (Security Review)
+**Date:** 2026-04-30
+**Reviewer:** Phase 8 agent (security review produced alongside implementation)
+
+---
+
+## 1. Production-Credential Audit
+
+| Check | Status | Evidence |
+|-------|--------|----------|
+| Production credential loaded from `TARGET_PROD_API_KEY` env var only | PASS | `app/core/auth.py` — `get_target_credentials()` reads env var; no fallback to hardcoded values |
+| Staging credential loaded from `TARGET_API_KEY` env var only | PASS | Same function, conditional on `environment` parameter |
+| No hardcoded API keys in source code | PASS | `git grep` for `sk_live_`, `sk_test_`, hardcoded key patterns returns zero matches in `app/` |
+| Credential not committed to repository | PASS | `.gitignore` does not need entry (env vars, not files) — verified no `.env` file committed |
+| Missing credential → fail-closed | PASS | `CredentialError` raised on missing/empty env var; no silent fallback |
+
+## 2. Read-Only API Access
+
+| Check | Status | Evidence |
+|-------|--------|----------|
+| `TargetFinanceClient` has no write methods | PASS | Only `fetch_payouts()` exists; no `create_*`, `update_*`, `delete_*`, `post_*`, `put_*`, `patch_*` methods |
+| Only `GET` HTTP method used | PASS | `httpx.AsyncClient.get()` is the sole HTTP call |
+| No request body sent | PASS | Query parameters only via `params=` kwarg |
+
+## 3. Zero Production API Calls in Tests
+
+| Check | Status | Evidence |
+|-------|--------|----------|
+| `respx` mock blocks all unmocked HTTP | PASS | `test_no_production_calls.py` — `respx.mock(assert_all_mocked=True)` used |
+| Zero outbound to `api.target.com` | PASS | Test assertion confirms 0 calls |
+| Zero outbound to `stage-api.target.com` | PASS | Test assertion confirms 0 calls |
+| HTTP client injected via DI | PASS | `TargetFinanceClient` constructor accepts `http_client` parameter for test injection |
+
+## 4. Stripe ID Redaction
+
+| Check | Status | Evidence |
+|-------|--------|----------|
+| Full Stripe IDs never logged | PASS | `poll.py` logs redacted form: suffix only (`payout_id[-4:]`) |
+| Log entries use structured fields | PASS | `logger.warning()` with `extra={}` dict, not string interpolation of IDs |
+
+## 5. SQL Injection Prevention
+
+| Check | Status | Evidence |
+|-------|--------|----------|
+| All queries via SQLAlchemy ORM | PASS | No raw SQL string interpolation in `app/finance/` |
+| Parameterized queries only | PASS | `session.execute(select(Payout).where(...))` patterns throughout |
+
+## 6. Production Credential Scope
+
+| Finding | Severity | Status |
+|---------|----------|--------|
+| Target's auth model does not document per-operation scoping (read vs write) | INFO | The API key grants access to all endpoints the seller_id is authorized for. Since `TargetFinanceClient` only issues `GET` requests, the risk is mitigated at the application layer, not the credential layer. |
+| Recommend: request Target to issue a read-only scoped credential if their API supports it | LOW | Escalation to Mark if Target offers credential scoping in future |
+
+---
+
+## Summary
+
+All security constraints from feature-spec § 9 are satisfied. The implementation is read-only, credentials are loaded exclusively from environment variables, and tests make zero outbound HTTP calls to Target API domains. Stripe IDs are redacted in all log output.
