+# Test Design — STORY-012: Target Finance/Settlement Ingest
+
+**Phase:** 7 (Test Design)
+**Date:** 2026-04-30
+**Status:** RED state verified — 50 passed, 41 xfailed, 0 errors
+
+---
+
+## Overview
+
+This document describes the test strategy for the Target Finance/Settlement ingest feature.
+Tests were written before implementation (TDD, Phase 7). All tests that exercise
+unimplemented logic are marked `@pytest.mark.xfail(strict=True)` so they report as
+XFAIL in RED state and will automatically turn GREEN when Phase 8 implements the logic.
+
+Structural tests (model schema, index definitions, regex constants, DI wiring) PASS now
+because those artifacts are already fully implemented.
+
+---
+
+## Test Counts (RED State)
+
+| Result  | Count | Notes                                                       |
+|---------|-------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
+| PASSED  | 50    | Structural/schema tests + integration smoke tests           |
+| XFAILED | 41    | Business logic tests — to be implemented in Phase 8         |
+| FAILED  | 0     | No unexpected failures                                      |
+| ERROR   | 0     | No import or fixture errors                                 |
+| **Total** | **91** |                                                           |
+
+---
+
+## File Map
+
+```
+tests/
+  conftest.py                      # Shared constants (SAMPLE_SELLER_ID, TEST_API_KEY)
+  finance/
+    conftest.py                    # DB engine, mock client, autouse patch fixture, sample data
+    test_models.py                 # Schema contract: 14 columns, indexes, smoke insert (PASS)
+    test_ingest.py                 # Core ingest cycle, poll_state, observability (XFAIL)
+    test_unknown_status.py         # status_known flagging, KNOWN_STATUSES constant (XFAIL)
+    test_dedup.py                  # Upsert idempotency, updated_at advance, NOT NULL gate (XFAIL)
+    test_xref.py                   # Index definitions + ORM cross-ref queries (PASS)
+    test_no_production_calls.py    # Gate 2a isolation, API degradation, failure recovery (mixed)
+    test_credential_audit.py       # Credential enforcement point, env var isolation (XFAIL)
+
+app/
+  __init__.py
+  core/
+    __init__.py
+    auth.py                        # TargetCredentials + get_target_credentials() stub
+  finance/
+    __init__.py
+    models.py                      # Full SQLAlchemy models — Payout (14 cols) + PollState
+    client.py                      # TargetFinanceClient stub + TargetAPIError
+    poll.py                        # ingest_once() stub + module-level DI hooks
+
+alembic/
+  alembic.ini
+  env.py
+  versions/
+    001_target_finance.py          # Migration skeleton: payouts + poll_state tables
+```
+
+---
+
+## Test Strategy
+
+### Fixture Architecture
+
+- **`test_engine`** (async, per-test): fresh `sqlite+aiosqlite:///:memory:` engine with
+  `Base.metadata.create_all`. Each test gets an isolated schema — no shared state.
+- **`async_session`** (async, per-test): `async_sessionmaker` session for direct DB
+  queries. Rolls back after each test.
+- **`mock_finance_client`** (sync, per-test): `MockTargetFinanceClient` spy — controls
+  `response`, records `calls`, simulates errors via `raise_on_next_call`.
+- **`setup_test_env`** (autouse async): patches `poll._engine` and `poll._client` with
+  the per-test fixtures. Also sets `TARGET_API_KEY` / `SELLER_ID` env vars as baseline.
+
+### xfail Discipline
+
+- `strict=True` means: if a test marked xfail actually passes, it becomes a hard FAILURE.
+  This prevents Phase 8 from leaving orphaned xfail markers after implementation.
+- Structural tests (models, regex, DI constructor, ORM queries) are NOT marked xfail
+  because they already pass against the implemented models.
+- One test (`test_api_failure_does_not_update_poll_state`) was initially marked xfail but
+  removed — the stub's "do nothing" behavior trivially satisfies the invariant, so the
+  test correctly PASSES now and will continue to pass when Phase 8 is implemented.
+
+---
+
+## Gates Covered
+
+| Gate | Test(s)                                                                        |
+|------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
+| 1    | `test_fetch_payouts_omits_none_params` — None params not sent as query strings |
+| 2a   | `test_no_outbound_calls_to_target_api_domain` — respx isolation, no real HTTP  |
+| 2b   | `test_client_raises_target_api_error_on_4xx/5xx/timeout` — error mapping       |
+| 3    | `test_all_not_null_columns_populated_on_insert` — NOT NULL constraint alignment |
+| 9    | `test_api_failure_does_not_persist_partial_results` — atomicity on failure      |
+| 10   | `test_ingest_success_logs_structured_fields` — structured log on success        |
+| 10   | `test_ingest_api_failure_logs_error_with_context` — error not silently swallowed|
+| 11   | `test_client_can_be_instantiated_with_required_args` — valid constructor fields |
+| 12   | `test_payout_row_can_be_inserted_and_queried` — ORM smoke insert round-trip    |
+
+---
+
+## Key Design Decisions
+
+### Output Variance Gate
+`test_ingest_output_varies_with_different_payloads` ensures a stub that always returns
+hardcoded `records_inserted=0` cannot pass — the implementation must actually count.
+
+### Decimal Precision
+`test_ingest_payout_amount_stored_as_exact_decimal` verifies `Decimal("1250.75")` is
+stored without float rounding error. The model uses `Numeric(12, 2)` to enforce this.
+
+### Stripe ID Advisory Validation
+`test_payout_with_invalid_stripe_id_is_still_persisted` codifies "warn + continue":
+financial records must never be dropped due to ID format changes by Target.
+
+### Credential Separation
+`test_staging_reads_target_api_key_env_var` and `test_production_reads_target_prod_api_key_env_var`
+enforce that staging and production keys come from different env vars, preventing
+accidental cross-environment key usage.
+
+### Poll State High-Water Mark
+`test_ingest_updates_poll_state_to_max_created_date` verifies the window advances to
+`max(created_date)`, not `now()`, so records with future-dated fields are not missed.
+
+---
+
+## Phase 8 Contract
+
+When Phase 8 implements `ingest_once()`, `TargetFinanceClient.fetch_payouts()`, and
+`get_target_credentials()`, the 41 xfailed tests must turn GREEN. No new tests should
+be needed for the base feature — any additional edge cases discovered during
+implementation should be added as new tests before fixing.
+
+The xfail markers must be removed from tests as they pass. If a test cannot be made to
+pass without changing its assertion, that signals a spec deviation requiring review.
